    Data Analyst / Business Analyst

        Where it is applied: Virtually any industry – Tech, Finance, E-commerce, Healthcare, Consulting, Retail, Government. Companies use data analysts to make informed decisions.

        Average salary range in Europe: €45,000 - €90,000 per year (Median approx. €60,000), depending on location, industry, and experience level.

        Useful skills: Strong analytical and quantitative skills (Maths/Stats), programming knowledge (SQL, Python, R are common), data visualization tools (e.g., Tableau, Power BI), business acumen, problem-solving, excellent communication skills (to explain findings to non-technical audiences). This aligns with your Math, Programming, and Business interests.

    Technical Project Manager

        Where it is applied: Technology companies (software, hardware), Engineering firms, Construction companies, Manufacturing, Consulting firms managing technical projects.

        Average salary range in Europe: €50,000 - €100,000+ per year (Median approx. €70,000), highly dependent on industry, project complexity, and experience.

        Useful skills: Excellent organizational and planning skills, leadership, communication (written and verbal), risk management, problem-solving, understanding of the technical field (Software Development life cycle, Engineering principles – your Math/Physics background is relevant here), budgeting, stakeholder management. This role capitalises on your organizing and communication talents and your technical aptitude.

